INT. GRAND HOTEL BALLROOM - MASQUERADE - NIGHT - 1961

Crystal chandeliers. A twenty-piece orchestra. Guests in feathered masks spin across a marble floor.

LADY VERA STANHOPE, 50s, in peacock silk, holds court by the champagne tower. MAXIMILIAN VOSS, 40s, in a Venetian bauta, waltzes with COLETTE DUPRE, 30s, in a cat mask. HOBBS, 60s, a butler, balances a tray. PERCIVAL, 30s, a young footman, stands by the cloakroom. ROSARIO ESPINOZA, 20s, a waitress, offers canapes.

All is calm. Violins swell.

Lady Vera lifts her glass. Maximilian dips Colette. The orchestra hits a crescendo. The lights flicker once.

The chandeliers go dark. Gasps. A single beam of moonlight from the skylight falls on Lady Vera's neck. Her diamond necklace is gone.

LADY VERA
My necklace!

Everyone freezes. Maximilian lets Colette fall. Hobbs drops the tray. Percival bolts for the door. Rosario hurls a canape. It splats against the chandelier. The lights flick on.

The necklace dangles from Colette's cat mask like a fish on a hook. She stands, mask askew, smiling.

COLETTE
Evening, Aunt Vera.
